    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the new `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` acceptance test.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nRejecting a new owner whose lower-cased email collides with any existing owner, responding **409 Conflict** \u2014 following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions and mirroring the existing duplicate-telephone rule.\n\n**New files:**\n- `rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueOwnerEmail.java` \u2014 pipeline step that canonicalizes the request email via the shared `OwnerEmails.normalize` (lower-case) rule, compares it case-insensitively against every existing owner's email, and throws `DuplicateEmailException` on a match. An absent/blank email is never a duplicate.\n- `rest/escalation/DuplicateEmailException.java` \u2014 checked exception (so it surfaces in `throws`).\n- `rest/escalation/DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds 409 with a `ProblemDetail`, matching the telephone handler.\n- `officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateEmailException.yml` \u2014 wires the handler.\n\n**Edited:**\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `ensureUniqueEmail` step (governed by `transaction`) between `ensureUniqueTelephone` and `ensureUniqueHousehold`.\n\nThe check reads the email off the already-validated `OwnerFieldsDto` request variable and compares both sides through the same normalization used when the email is stored, so it's independent of the casing either value was supplied in.",
