        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into an established family of patterns and introduces no duplication or catch-all classes.\n\n- **Mirrors the existing `EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone` family exactly.** `EnsureUniqueOwnerEmail`, `DuplicateEmailException`, and `DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler` are structurally identical to their telephone/household counterparts (same `service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto, OwnerRepository)` signature, same `ProblemDetails.build(..., CONFLICT, ...)` handler body, same exception message shape). A maintainer who knows the telephone check will read the email one instantly.\n- **Reuses the shared rule rather than duplicating it.** Normalization goes through the existing `OwnerEmails.normalize` (the documented single source of truth for lower-casing), matching how the telephone check delegates to `OwnerTelephones`. No canonicalization logic is re-inlined.\n- **Logic is in the right unit.** One small function per step, the uniqueness concern isn't folded into `BuildOwner` or `ValidateOwner`, and the error path uses the YAML escalation + handler convention per AGENTS.md rather than inline status handling.\n- **Wiring is coherent.** The new `ensureUniqueEmail` step is inserted between `ensureUniqueTelephone` and `ensureUniqueHousehold`, grouping it with the other uniqueness guards and carrying the same `govern: [ transaction ]` as its neighbors.\n- The added absent/blank guard (which the telephone version lacks) is an appropriate, intentional difference since email is optional \u2014 not an inconsistency worth flagging."
